  "rules": [
    "When recent history shows a strong downtrend (e.g., Example 1 & 2) and sentiment is neutral or slightly negative, the model systematically overestimates future prices by ignoring immediate mean reversion; apply a downward correction of 5-8% to forecasted values.",
    "When recent history shows a volatile uptrend with positive sentiment spikes (e.g., Examples 3 & 4), the model fails to capture momentum and underestimates price surges; apply an upward correction proportional to the last 3 days' volatility increase.",
    "The model exhibits significant lag in reacting to sudden sentiment shifts (e.g., Example 5's final positive spike); forecasts remain flat while true outcomes surge, requiring a dynamic multiplier based on the most recent sentiment change direction.",
    "In high-volatility regimes, the model assumes linear growth but actual outcomes show erratic spikes followed by sharp corrections; reduce forecast confidence and widen prediction bands by 10-15%."
  ]
}
